      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, the parser shouldn\u0027t depend on the NOT state. The counter was originally there to cancel out pairs of NOTs, but using a boolean toggle would have been a better approach.\n\nInstead of adding a Simplify phase, I\u0027d prefer to reject chained NOTs. In patchset 17, the parser builds the AST as written and rejects a NOT that is not followed by TRUE, FALSE or a D-Bus probe, so chained NOTs (e.g. `NOT NOT A`) is rejected.\n\nChained NOTs have no practical use in a configuration, and since the other possible simplification would bring little benefit, `NOT(NOT(A))` -\u003e `A` as the only rule in the Simplify phase.\n\nRejecting chained NOTs allows us to keep the existing pipeline:\nString -\u003e Lexer -\u003e Tokens -\u003e Parser -\u003e AST -\u003e Evaluate -\u003e Result\n\nDoes that work for you, or would you prefer to keep the chained NOTs and\nadd Simplify phase?",
      "parentUuid": "81badaeb_06183fa2",
